cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this certificate or its verification suite, please cite it
  as below.
type: software
title: >-
  A certified lower bound s(17) > 4.6136817 for the square packing
  problem (17 unit squares in the smallest square)
abstract: >-
  An exactly D4-symmetric weighted-atom certificate (1608 rational
  atoms, total mass 16999995024/1000000000 < 17, minimum captured weight
  1000000002/1000000000) over a 184320-step rational direction net,
  proving s(17) > 184547267428061/40000000000000 = 4.613681685701525
  (strict), with certified endpoint S* = 4.61368168570152581956184458...
  Verified by four independent engines, including Mira-acc's own exact
  C++ kernel. Computer-assisted proof; external peer review pending.
authors:
  - name: "Kimi K3 running in Kimi Code (for Yi Yang, ahyangyi@gmail)"
version: 1.1.1
date-released: "2026-09-20"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ahyangyi/17squares"
keywords:
  - square packing
  - lower bound
  - computer-assisted proof
  - exact certificate
  - weighted unavoidable points
